{
  "label": "Rule metadata display",
  "category": "Rules",
  "description": "How the Other metadata of a rule page shows known keys: label and Font Awesome icon per key (keys not listed get their own name and a generic icon). Keys starting with one of hash_prefixes are shown as hashes (monospace, copy button). A value that is a comma-separated list of short items (\"mirai,gafgyt,tsunami\", \"Cobalt Strike, Mimikatz\") is shown one item per line when split_comma_lists is true; sentences with commas are left whole. Each field may have a style: \"badge\" (each value a coloured chip, tone: red / orange / gold / green / teal / blue / purple / gray), \"scale\" (the colour depends on the value, from scales.<name>, e.g. high / medium / low; a number from 0 to 100 shows a gauge) or \"meter\" (a number from 0 to 100, or 0 to 10, as a gauge). Style \"tlp\" (TLP, PAP, sharing): the value shown as an official TLP 2.0 label — coloured text on black: RED, AMBER (AMBER+STRICT), GREEN, CLEAR; \"TLP:\" / \"PAP:\" prefixes and case are ignored. platforms = keywords recognised in any metadata value (Windows, Linux, AWS, GitHub…; whole words, case ignored, first match wins): the value is shown with the platform's logo (Font Awesome brand icon) and colour. A platform's details = {keyword: name}: the part shown under it (Windows → Sysmon, PowerShell…; the rules list filters on the platform or on one detail).",
